WEBVTT

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.300
The Isuzu League, eh?

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.100
Chimera Clausen is abducting spirits
in the southern part of the continent.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.310
We don't have a good grasp
of the realities, either,

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:24.810
but their numbers aren't small.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.560
We also don't know what they're
doing with the abducted spirits.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.940
But with your help, we were able
to capture one of their members.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:34.150
This may allow us to
figure out their objective.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.780
You have our thanks.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.450
If they are a group that protects spirits,

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.540
they may know about Kagura as well.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.710
I will pay them a visit at some point.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.370
Deep in thought, meow?

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:48.840
Hm? Oh, nothing of great importance.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.800
More importantly,
let us take a little break.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.170
"Distracted driving causes accidents"

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.130
Ah, caravans.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:00.060
If they have something interesting,
it will serve as a souvenir.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.350
Mira.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:09.020
Ah! You lot! Why are you here?

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.150
Mira!

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.490
Take that!

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.320
Meow! Two! Three!

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:18.950
"Taught by Karl Gotch himself"

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:18.950
And stay down!

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:21.620
Nothing has changed, I see.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.800
"Episode 11
'Did... None of the Praise Come My Way?'"
And now, here's to a safe
and sound reunion.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.800
"Episode 11
'Did... None of the Praise Come My Way?'"
Cheers!

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.600
Ah! The honey au lait here is perfection!

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.430
Oh! The liquid that just
went into Mira's mouth

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:08.140
is trickling down into her body...

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.310
Bam!

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.770
Escorting a caravan is very
nice and adventurer-like.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:13.690
It is, right?

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:17.440
However, escorts invariably
come under attack.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.200
Unfortunately, we don't seem
to have triggered it yet.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.740
I see.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.700
Are the others all in good health?

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:30.540
Yes. Asval is separate, because
he's with the second contingent,

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.830
but Zef is here.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:34.670
Oh, yeah! And Tact is doing well, too.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:38.000
He's studying to become a priest now.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.170
That is wonderful to hear.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.970
And you are getting close.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:43.180
Ouch!

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.300
Mira, is that...

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.010
...a pure rabbit?

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:49.890
Mm, as fate would have it,
we became friends.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.610
"Tequila Meowrise"

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.610
Non-alcoholic, meow.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.700
Are you all heading west?

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.870
Yes, the plan is to go through
the forest to Osstein.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:07.200
Is there something to the west?

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.120
Two things.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:14.540
One, I fought a tyrant spikeback
in the Child of Prayer Forest.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:17.000
Isn't that a monster of the Ark Continent?

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.460
It ought to be, yes.

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:24.050
And one other thing. Do you know
of a group called Chimera Clausen?

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:27.550
Yes, we've received some
information from the Union.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:29.850
That saves me from having to explain.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.810
Yesterday, I captured a member
of Chimera Clausen

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:35.190
and left him with members
of an opposing organization.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:40.110
His fellow Chimera members may just
show up to rescue one of their own.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:43.110
We had better be vigilant then.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:44.950
Thank you very much.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:49.780
But you certainly do stick your
nose into all kinds of trouble.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.830
Such is the fate of an adventurer.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:55.420
And here is some useful information
for Mira the adventurer.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:57.540
Hm? Oh-ho!

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:24.190
"Closed for the Day"

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:30.200
A ghost ship, a castle in the sky,
and an underground city of gold!

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.370
Interesting indeed!

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:35.790
Mira with her eyes sparkling at the
thought of as yet unseen adventures!

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.420
I want to eat you up!

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.000
Oh, no, you don't!

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.630
Tell me, Cyril, is there anything else?

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:43.590
Let me think.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:47.260
Oh, this isn't quite the same as a rumor,

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.890
but have you heard of the
City of the Hero in Black?

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:52.060
The City of the Hero in Black, you say?

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:53.310
Yes.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.310
It was about ten years ago now,

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:57.980
right around the time of the Defense
of the Three Great Kingdoms.

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:00.980
It seems a city in the northern
part of the Earth Continent

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.520
was attacked by a horde of demons.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:07.610
This city had no means to
stand against powerful demons

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:09.910
and could only suffer
the devastation in silence.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:14.120
That was when it happened.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.540
A lone hero appeared in the city

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:20.630
and they say he instantly reduced
the demons to cinders.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:33.180
Some among the demons apparently
even had title and rank,

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:36.060
but it seems they were no match for him.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.560
Afterwards, the hero who saved the city

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:41.560
left without even revealing his name.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:44.980
This man dressed entirely in black
was lauded as the Hero in Black

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:48.570
and that city is now known as
the City of the Hero in Black.

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:50.950
The Hero in Black, eh?

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:54.370
That is unmistakably Valentin.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:58.080
Shy and not good at talking to people.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.750
He likes being appreciated, but cannot
accept gratitude face-to-face.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:06.250
Socially awkward in the extreme,
even among us Nine Wise Men.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:09.630
Is something the matter?

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:12.760
No, I just remembered something.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:16.770
The City of the Hero in Black, eh?
I must make my way there eventually.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:17.890
Captain!

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:20.020
Wait. Mira?

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:22.150
It has been a while, Zef.

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:23.900
Have you been good?

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:25.980
Wait, there's no time for that!

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:28.070
We need to hurry to see the caravan chief!

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:31.700
It looks like a unit in the back
was attacked by monsters!

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.030
I understand.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:34.530
Well, then, Mira...

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:36.200
I will come as well.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.120
I find this a tad troubling.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.920
The one who was attacked was the last
wagon, Noland with Unit 8, right?

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:50.670
Yes, I pursued the monsters
who took the cargo,

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.970
but there were more of them
swarming about than I'd ever seen,

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:55.140
so I had no choice but to turn back.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:59.140
Provisions were being transported
by Units 5, 6, and 7, right?

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:00.850
Why attack Unit 8?

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:02.600
I wonder what it was carrying.

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:05.940
If I remember right,
it was pieces of stone.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:08.650
Caravan Chief, we'll go.

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:10.150
Please do.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:13.200
Mm, then shall we go?

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.990
Cyril, who is that?

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:18.620
A very dependable ally.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:29.130
Do you suppose it was Noland?

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:30.550
Let us hurry.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:44.890
Huh? What?

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:45.980
When did she even...

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:47.810
Mira, you're amazing!

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:50.780
Oh...

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.190
As impressive as ever.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:54.400
Was that presumptuous of me?

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.700
Oh, no, you were a big help.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:57.950
More importantly...

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:59.660
This monster...

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:02.750
Mm, not one to be seen in these parts.

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:05.210
There.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.500
You saved me, Cyril.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:10.170
Please, I'm just glad you're all right.

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:11.170
What of the cargo?

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:14.010
They took it deeper into the woods.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.430
I understand.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:19.600
Please return to the caravan
and leave the rest to us.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:21.720
Thank you very much.

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:24.140
But these woods are...

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:32.110
The further you go in,
the denser the fog grows

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:35.150
and the more monsters attack you, he said.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:37.070
Not only that, but for some reason...

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:39.070
We keep coming back to this spot.

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:41.330
This is clearly not normal.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:42.910
We're looping.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:46.080
And without arousing
our suspicions at that.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:51.670
I think this is the time to
call in some specialists.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:00.600
Mira, what is this?

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:05.980
They are Korpokkurs, kin to spirits
and experts on the land and woods.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:09.060
It has been a long time,
it has, Village Chief.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.560
Yo, Village Chief.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:15.990
Village Chief!

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:18.320
Oh, mm.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.160
Uneko, you seem unchanged
and that puts me at ease.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.870
Yes, indeed, yes.

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:26.450
And would I be correct in
assuming you are Etenoir?

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:31.080
Oh, 'course, it's me! That's hilarious!

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:34.590
How to put this? You seem to have
become terribly sophisticated.

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:37.720
Nah, well, it's not like it's that weird.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.010
More like, shouldn't we
be talking about you?

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:42.260
You totes went all the way
with your makeover.

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:44.640
You are not to make mention of it.

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:47.980
I mean, this style might be something
you could pull off, Sis Uneko.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.850
All frilly and sweet.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:52.610
I feel comfortable in
my usual outfit, I feel.

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:53.820
And besides,

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:57.570
it would be disrespectful to be dressed
the same as the Village Chief.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:00.410
What? Wearing matching outfits is fun!

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:02.200
Right, Village Chief?

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:07.290
Hm? Well, I see nothing wrong with
trying out various outfits, but...

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:10.370
No, it is not good to force these things.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.000
I had no idea that this was
what Korpokkurs were like.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.750
So cute!

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.710
Is this what they call
"individual differences"?

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:18.470
Um, Mira?

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:20.010
Uh, oh, that is right!

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:23.430
Uneko, Etenoir, I have a request for you.

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:25.310
Please ask whatever you like of us.

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:26.470
R!

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:27.520
"R"?

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.640
R for "roger that"!

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:32.980
So, this is what 30 years does to someone.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:50.500
How did it go, Uneko? Etenoir?

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:55.460
Village Chief, we cannot sense
any spirits in these woods.

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:59.300
The spirits who maintain the
circulation of mana are absent?

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:00.720
Is that possible?

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:02.380
It's totes impossible.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:08.520
As I recall, they are the ones
capturing spirits from all over.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:12.980
We hear that some places are already
experiencing disturbances due to this.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:17.900
There seems little room for doubt
that Chimera Clausen caused this.

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:19.650
Now, then...

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:21.610
What to do?

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:23.410
We can't leave matters as is.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:25.200
Let us fix this.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.740
Yes, let's get this done,
you and us together.

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:30.290
There's no way we can turn a blind eye.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:33.250
Mm, then it is decided.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.710
We are counting on you, Uneko, Etenoir.

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:39.050
Yes! We found where
the flow of mana is sluggish.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:42.050
Well, this kind of thing
is a piece of cake.

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:51.730
Then, shall we go?

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:56.230
Ah, it seems we have arrived.

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:02.070
Yes, it does.

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:03.570
Hold on a second!

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:06.070
This many has got to be a bad idea!

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:11.040
I see what appears to be the cargo, but...

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.670
Could it be that those are...

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:20.800
The Ash Silver Lion and the Golden Lion.

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:24.380
What a surprise to see
even legendary beasts.

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:29.010
Which would you like?

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:31.060
I think I will take the Golden Lion.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:34.060
Then I will take the Ash Silver Lion.

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:40.980
The Captain and them are going for it.

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:42.320
It can't be helped.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:45.450
Shall we take care of the small fry?

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:46.450
Well, then...

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:48.110
Let the show begin.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:29.860
Well, well, this one is quite energetic.

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:33.830
More than good enough if they can
repel a legendary beast's attack.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.750
"Immortal Arts: Refined Thrust"

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:53.010
This is the end.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.440
Not too bad.

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:05.280
Combining partial summons
with immortal arts spells...

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:07.150
I am starting to get used to it.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:18.460
Brilliantly done.

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:21.330
Oh, no, I still have a long way to go.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:23.790
Now, then, as for the others...

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:35.890
Let me see...

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:38.520
Please limit your aid to
the absolute minimum.

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:39.640
Are you sure?

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:40.980
Yes.

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:45.270
Because I want those youngsters
to grow stronger.

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:53.910
I suppose the things that
occur to us are the same.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:55.490
Roger that.

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:00.410
Fight well!

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:24.060
Could this be part of the cargo?

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:28.570
They were after this?

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:31.990
This...

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:35.820
The pattern looks similar to
the Demon's Blessing, but...

00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:50.510
This place...

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:56.260
Might I trouble you for a moment?

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:59.180
Well, this is an unexpected visitor.

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:02.390
So, what might you wish to talk about?

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:08.360
Everyone who comes to this era
gets that look on their face.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:10.690
My apologies. Somehow...

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:12.280
Your senses are dulled?

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:13.530
You can tell?

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:15.110
In a manner of speaking.

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:16.990
You said, "this era."

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:19.280
Mightn't you tell me more about it?

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.290
Sure, I don't mind.

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:25.500
A past era?

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:28.960
Yes, you were caught in
a distortion in space-time

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:31.500
and only your soul traveled into the past.

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:33.510
Oh, you don't have to worry.

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:36.010
You'll be able to go back
after a little while.

00:17:36.010 --> 00:17:37.140
I see.

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:40.640
But I do think something must have
triggered your coming here.

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:41.930
Does anything come to mind?

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:43.680
Let me think...

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:51.400
I touched an odd stone tablet in
a forest with stagnant mana, but...

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:52.820
That must have been it.

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:54.940
Oh, I see.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:57.280
The distortion in the mana
interfered with space-time

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:59.450
and created the wrinkle in time.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:03.830
And that stone tablet must have
served as your guide to this time.

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:07.080
So, mana can even affect space-time.

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:09.960
Mana is both zero and one.

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:14.260
It's also the pillar that ensures
that space remains space.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:17.680
This is the concept of
mana among our people.

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:19.510
Both zero and one, is it?

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:21.720
That is an interesting thought.

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:24.560
There's something
that bothers me a little.

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:28.400
A mana distortion great enough
to interfere with space-time is rare.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:30.520
I hope this will be the end of it, but...

00:18:30.520 --> 00:18:32.860
You are saying something
more may yet happen?

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:36.530
It may and it may not.

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:39.780
I will take that as a warning.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:42.080
You seem terribly knowledgeable,

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:44.660
but just who are you people?

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:48.960
We are the Devils.

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.540
Devils, you say?

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:52.750
It sounds like you've heard of us.

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:57.840
No, when it comes to Devils, in our era,
it is the Devils' Labyrinths.

00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:01.890
Really? Labyrinths that bear our name?

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:03.760
They sound interesting.

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:07.730
They are some terribly
idiosyncratic labyrinths, but...

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:08.600
Oh?

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:11.270
Oh, it looks like you can go back already.

00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:12.690
Is that so?

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:14.860
I would've liked to
talk to you a little more,

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:17.320
but I kind of have a feeling that
we'll meet again, so... Oh, well.

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:18.900
What is that supposed to mean?

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:23.280
Tell me, just where are you people headed?

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:25.910
The Reincarnation Gate.

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:29.120
We're going to be reborn as a new species.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:32.130
Just what will you turn into?

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:33.590
Angels.

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:35.880
Angels?

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:39.170
Then, that black gate is...

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:42.680
It's...

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:48.100
What's the matter, Mira?

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:51.480
Mm, oh, nothing.

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:53.690
We're done taking care of the monsters.

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:55.900
Let's retrieve the cargo and go back.

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:57.530
Yes.

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:07.330
I feel like I was talking
to someone, but...

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:09.700
Was it just my imagination?

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:27.640
Please be careful on your travels.

00:20:27.640 --> 00:20:29.930
See you later, Mira.

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:32.770
Don't stick your nose into
anything too dangerous.

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:36.110
I haven't gotten enough Mira!

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:41.860
Cyril. Emella. Zef. And Flicker.

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:44.320
You be careful on your travels.

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:06.760
What is that?

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:15.020
What in the world...

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:19.520
That is...

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:20.860
Miss Mira.

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:23.070
Garrett, what is going on?

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:24.530
A horde of monsters.

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:25.740
What did you say?

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:28.450
A horde of monsters appeared
within the kingdom's borders.

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.290
And one of an unprecedented size.

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:40.590
I broke through the ranks
of the horde of monsters

00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:43.550
in order to inform you of this.

00:21:43.550 --> 00:21:47.550
Miss Mira, please join King Solomon
as quickly as you can.

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:53.180
A mana distortion great enough
to interfere with space-time is rare.

00:21:53.180 --> 00:21:55.810
I hope this will be the end of it, but...

00:21:55.810 --> 00:21:57.270
I understand.

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:01.150
However...

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:19.960
I am sure he would not mind
if I cleaned up here a bit first.
